WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.640
- But wait.

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:02.473
So when we talk last,

00:00:02.473 --> 00:00:03.540
you were planning a
vacation with your in-laws.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:04.470
- [Seth] Yeah.
- So how did that go?

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.790
- I spent a lot of summer with my in-laws.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.352
I hit the jackpot with my in-laws.

00:00:08.352 --> 00:00:09.185
- [Kelly] I've heard you say this.

00:00:09.185 --> 00:00:10.018
- They're wonderful.

00:00:10.018 --> 00:00:11.370
They're incredible grandparents.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.560
And they do a thing,

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.610
it's really special to me,

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.950
which is they love their
daughter as much as I do.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.670
But there are a few times when
my wife and I are fighting,

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.020
my in-laws will take my side,
(audience gasps)

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.090
not verbally

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.550
but you know when you're
having a fight with a spouse

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.870
sometimes this means the world.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.620
They'll just do their thing
and then look at me and go.

00:00:31.709 --> 00:00:33.060
(audience laughs)

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.180
And it's like that just
helps you get through it.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.013
They're basically saying,

00:00:37.013 --> 00:00:37.846
look-
- You're not alone.

00:00:37.846 --> 00:00:40.710
- I can't jump in and
take the brunt of this.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.297
I am ultimately a coward.

00:00:42.297 --> 00:00:43.850
(audience laughs)

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:44.940
but I want you to know that,

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.440
hearing both sides of this fight,

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.880
I realize that you're right.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.160
And I want to roll my
eyes at you to give you

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.750
just that connection-
- That's nice.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.090
Just the connection of not
feeling alone on an island.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.410
- It's very special.
- Yes

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.520
But then you're also frustrated

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.590
cause you're like, say something.

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:00.930
- Well, I am not that frustrated

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.880
because my wife will often,

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.890
not often, but sometimes
fight with her parents

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.510
and then I will do the same thing.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.400
I won't actually jump in and help.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.360
But I will then look at them

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.460
and give them the return, like...

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.540
- Maybe this is my issue.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.890
I'm way too honest.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.300
Maybe that's my...(laughs)
- Oh yeah.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.160
Honesty's a real dead end.
- That gets you nowhere.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.180
- Yeah.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.860
I can't believe you've
been an honest person

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.120
in show business and done so well

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:21.953
for yourself.
- I know. (laughing)

00:01:21.953 --> 00:01:22.786
It's a fluke.
- It really speaks

00:01:22.786 --> 00:01:23.619
to your talents.

00:01:23.619 --> 00:01:24.452
- It's a fluke. (laughing)
- It really speaks

00:01:24.452 --> 00:01:25.285
to your talents.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.118
Yeah.

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:27.364
- Yeah. I dunno. (laughing)

00:01:27.364 --> 00:01:28.890
(audience laughs and cheers)

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:31.860
But you told us how last
time you lied to your dad.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.150
So I'm wondering if you're...

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.800
Oh, fine.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.530
I know, is Gloria like
"Holy, this is my work."

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.700
And I'm gonna like...

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.710
Should I just the whole time?

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:42.240
Am I gonna be Beyonce-
- We're gonna...

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.073
- this entire interview?

00:01:43.073 --> 00:01:45.949
(audience cheers)

00:01:45.949 --> 00:01:48.720
I was like, I know, I look
like Blake Shelton on stage

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.553
at a concert.

00:01:49.553 --> 00:01:50.730
(audience laughs)
I'm sweating

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.050
so much right now.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:52.920
It's fine.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:53.880
Everything's fine.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:54.713
- [Seth] Yeah.

00:01:54.713 --> 00:01:55.620
- I'll do it low.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.600
But no, but you told us... I
have a fan now, (Seth laughs)

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.890
for camera's sake, I'm gonna say this.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.560
I have a fan now because
I'm sweating my behind off.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:02.550
- Yeah.
- So, yep.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:03.383
I'm gonna look like Beyonce

00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:04.216
this entire interview.

00:02:04.216 --> 00:02:06.272
Here we go. I'm gonna do it
like this too. (Seth laughs)

00:02:06.272 --> 00:02:07.296
So...

00:02:07.296 --> 00:02:09.322
(Audience cheers)
You told us

00:02:09.322 --> 00:02:11.790
that you lied to your dad the last time

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:12.623
that we talked.

00:02:12.623 --> 00:02:14.610
So wait, has your son,
does he lie to you now?

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:18.240
- The five-year-old is a liar,
(audience laughs)

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.871
but he developed, it's
just like a human thing

00:02:21.871 --> 00:02:23.250
to develop.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:26.640
Like, he's done this
thing now where he'll say

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.050
he's having a nightmare.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.540
And then when you start
asking questions about

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.280
what the nightmare was-
- Yes.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.610
- he kind of moves on to like,
"I will tell you about that,

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.790
but there is this toy
helicopter," and you're like

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.770
is this, was this whole
thing cause you wanted

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.720
to talk about a toy helicopter
at four in the morning?

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:43.920
So that's where we're starting

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.300
to sense this.
- I'm wondering

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.470
if it's like a little boy thing,

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.180
cause my little girl is terrified,

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.013
kind of, to lie.

00:02:49.013 --> 00:02:50.670
She'll tell on herself, she's terrified.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.770
My son will in your face,

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.180
you've just watched him do it,

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.611
say, "I did not do it."

00:02:55.611 --> 00:02:56.910
(audience laughs)
- Yeah.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:00.030
- And I am like, you know what,
points for bold, being bold.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.490
- The three year old
has, is without guile,

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.560
so he's incapable of lying.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.037
So it's really fun when we'll say,

00:03:06.037 --> 00:03:07.800
"Do not get up from the table,

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.210
I'm telling you not to
get up at the table."

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.932
And he'll just say like,
"I'm gonna break the rules."

00:03:11.932 --> 00:03:13.200
(audience laughs)

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.077
- That's funny.
- So he's like,

00:03:14.077 --> 00:03:17.901
"I know, I hear you, but I'm
not gonna listen to you."

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.382
(audience laughs)

00:03:19.382 --> 00:03:20.365
- (laughing) "I do not respect you."

00:03:20.365 --> 00:03:21.265
- (laughing) Yeah.

